IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`

-- g2-art6-purposes.l4: Article 6 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Charitable purposes: the heads, their clarifications, the States' power to add to them, its limit, and the exclusion of
-- political purposes.  Group G2.  Imports only prelude, daydate, domain and `g2-nouns`.  No section GIVEN.
--
-- HOW A PURPOSE IS CLASSIFIED.  Which head of Article 6(1) a purpose falls under is a JUDGEMENT ("may reasonably be regarded as analogous" in (p) is the plainest case), so domain.l4 makes the head
-- a field of `Purpose`: `head`.  This module reads `head` as the caller's determination of the head, and then applies what the Law itself says about the heads: the clarifications of
-- Article 6(2) that NARROW head (h) (sport must involve physical skill and exertion) and head (i) (only facilities for people in need or open to the public at large), that EXTEND heads (d), (f)
-- and (n), and that deem a philosophical belief analogous to religion for (p); and the exclusion of Article 6(5).  The narrowing and extending clauses need facts that `Purpose` does not carry,
-- so they are read from `Facts about a purpose under Article 6` (g2-nouns; nouns request N1 of FRAGMENT-G2.md).  Nothing is computed from the words of a purpose.
-- The rules are written in the Law's order (6(1) to 6(5)); a rule may use a rule written further down, which L4 allows.

§ `Part 3 — Charity Test`

§§ `Article 6 — Charitable purposes`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Named refusals: a fact that a clause needs and the caller has not stated
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref Article 6(2)(c) (src:189)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(2)(c) was not given whether the sport involves physical skill and exertion` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(2)(c) was not given whether the sport involves physical skill and exertion"

@ref Article 6(2)(d) (src:190-192)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(2)(d) was not given whether the facilities or activities are primarily for people in need or open to the public at large` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(2)(d) was not given whether the facilities or activities are primarily for people in need or open to the public at large"

@ref Article 6(1)(i) (src:176)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life"

@ref Article 6(1)(l) (src:179)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity"

@ref Article 6(2)(c) and (d) (src:189-192)
GIVEN fact IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` fact MEANS
    CONSIDER fact
    WHEN JUST stated THEN stated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref Article 6(2)(c) and (d) (src:189-192)
GIVEN fact IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` fact MEANS
    CONSIDER fact
    WHEN JUST stated THEN NOT stated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 6(1) — The charitable purposes are the following`

-- src:167 | (1) For the purposes of this Law, the charitable purposes are –
-- src:168 | (a) the prevention or relief of poverty;
-- src:169 | (b) the advancement of education;
-- src:170 | (c) the advancement of religion;
-- src:171 | (d) the advancement of health;
-- src:172 | (e) the saving of lives;
-- src:173 | (f) the advancement of citizenship or community development;
-- src:174 | (g) the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science;
-- src:175 | (h) the advancement of public participation in sport;
-- src:176 | (i) the provision of recreational facilities, or the organisation of recreational activities, with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom the facilities or activities are primarily intended;
-- src:177 | (j) the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation;
-- src:178 | (k) the promotion of religious or racial harmony;
-- src:179 | (l) the promotion of equality and diversity;
-- src:180 | (m) the advancement of environmental protection or improvement;
-- src:181 | (n) the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage;
-- src:182 | (o) the advancement of animal welfare;
-- src:183 | (p) any other purpose that may reasonably be regarded as analogous to any of the purposes listed in sub-paragraphs (a) to (o).

-- Whether the head under which a purpose is recorded admits it.  Sixteen heads are listed, plus any that Regulations under Article 6(3) have added.  Three heads carry a clause that
-- narrows or joins them: (h) sport, (i) recreation (its own object, and 6(2)(d)), (l) equality and diversity; every other head admits a purpose recorded under it.
@ref Article 6(1) (src:167-183)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
      head IS A `Head of charitable purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the head admits the purpose` interp facts head MEANS
    CONSIDER head
    WHEN `the prevention or relief of poverty` THEN TRUE                                               -- (a)
    WHEN `the advancement of education` THEN TRUE                                                      -- (b)
    WHEN `the advancement of religion` THEN TRUE                                                       -- (c)
    WHEN `the advancement of health` THEN TRUE                                                         -- (d), extended by 6(2)(a)
    WHEN `the saving of lives` THEN TRUE                                                               -- (e)
    WHEN `the advancement of citizenship or community development` THEN TRUE                          -- (f), extended by 6(2)(b)
    WHEN `the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science` THEN TRUE                         -- (g)
    WHEN `the advancement of public participation in sport` THEN `Art 6(2)(c) sport means sport that involves physical skill and exertion` facts     -- (h), narrowed by 6(2)(c)
    WHEN `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities` THEN `Art 6(1)(i) paragraph (1)(i) is met` facts  -- (i), with its object, limited by 6(2)(d)
    WHEN `the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation` THEN TRUE            -- (j)
    WHEN `the promotion of religious or racial harmony` THEN TRUE                                      -- (k)
    WHEN `the promotion of equality and diversity` THEN `Art 6(1)(l) the purpose promotes equality and diversity` interp facts    -- (l)
    WHEN `the advancement of environmental protection or improvement` THEN TRUE                        -- (m)
    WHEN `the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` THEN TRUE   -- (n), extended by 6(2)(e)
    WHEN `the advancement of animal welfare` THEN TRUE                                                 -- (o)
    WHEN `any other purpose that may reasonably be regarded as analogous to one of the above` THEN TRUE   -- (p), a judgement the caller makes by recording this head
    WHEN `a purpose added by Regulations under Article 6(3)` label THEN TRUE                           -- a sub-paragraph added by Regulations under Article 6(3)

-- Paragraph (l) joins two ideas with "and".  FORK F2.11: both must be promoted (taken: the drafter wrote "or" in (j) and (k) and "and" here), or either suffices.
@ref Article 6(1)(l) (src:179)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(l) the purpose promotes equality and diversity` interp facts MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how equality and diversity is read`
    WHEN `a purpose must promote both equality and diversity`
        THEN `reading A of Article 6(1)(l): both are promoted` (facts's `the purpose promotes equality`) (facts's `the purpose promotes diversity`)
    WHEN `a purpose that promotes either equality or diversity suffices`
        THEN `reading B of Article 6(1)(l): either suffices` (facts's `the purpose promotes equality`) (facts's `the purpose promotes diversity`)

@ref Article 6(1)(l) (src:179)
GIVEN equality IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      diversity IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reading A of Article 6(1)(l): both are promoted` equality diversity MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` equality THEN FALSE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` diversity THEN FALSE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` equality AND `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` diversity THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity`

@ref Article 6(1)(l) (src:179)
GIVEN equality IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      diversity IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reading B of Article 6(1)(l): either suffices` equality diversity MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` equality THEN TRUE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` diversity THEN TRUE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` equality AND `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` diversity THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity`

-- Paragraph (i) has two conditions.  Its own words: "with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom the facilities or activities are primarily intended".
-- And 6(2)(d): it "applies only in relation to" facilities or activities for people in need or open to the public at large.  Both must hold.  If the object is stated not to hold, the
-- head does not admit the purpose, whatever 6(2)(d) says; if it is stated to hold, 6(2)(d) decides; if it is not stated, the head still does not admit the purpose when 6(2)(d) is
-- stated not to hold on both alternatives, and otherwise the encoding refuses.
@ref Article 6(1)(i), Article 6(2)(d) (src:176) (src:190-192)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1)(i) paragraph (1)(i) is met` facts MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` (facts's `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended`) THEN FALSE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` (facts's `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended`) THEN `Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` facts
        IF `Art 6(2)(d) both alternatives are stated as false` facts THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life`

-- A purpose falls within a paragraph of 6(1) if a clarification of 6(2) brings it there, or 6(2)(f) deems it analogous, or the head it is recorded under admits it.
-- The order matters only for refusals: a clarification that already decides the case is reached before a head that would have to refuse.
@ref Article 6(1), Article 6(2) (src:167-194)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      purpose IS A Purpose
      facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the purpose falls within a paragraph of paragraph (1)` interp purpose facts MEANS
        `Art 6(2) a clarification brings the purpose within a head` facts
    OR  `Art 6(2)(f) the purpose is analogous to the advancement of religion by the analogy of paragraph (1)(p)` purpose
    OR  `Art 6(1) the recorded head admits the purpose` interp purpose facts

@ref Article 6(1) (src:167-183)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      purpose IS A Purpose
      facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the recorded head admits the purpose` interp purpose facts MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose's head
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST recorded THEN `Art 6(1) the head admits the purpose` interp facts recorded

-- Article 6(1) together with 6(2) and 6(5): is the purpose a charitable purpose?  A purpose excluded by 6(5) is not, "irrespective of whether it would otherwise fall within paragraph (1)".
@ref Article 6(1), Article 6(5) (src:167-183) (src:201)
@export Whether a purpose is a charitable purpose under Article 6(1), as clarified by Article 6(2) and excluded by Article 6(5), on the readings chosen by the interpretation; the head recorded for the purpose is the caller's determination
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the fields read here are how a philosophical belief is placed and how equality and diversity is read
      purpose IS A Purpose
        @desc The purpose, with the head of Article 6(1) it falls under (a determination) and the flags of domain.l4
      facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
        @desc The facts that Article 6(2) reads about the purpose; use NOTHING for a fact that is not relevant to the purpose's head
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` interp purpose facts MEANS
        NOT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` purpose
    AND `Art 6(1) the purpose falls within a paragraph of paragraph (1)` interp purpose facts

-- The pair form, for the list of an entity's purposes.
@ref Article 6(1) (src:167-183)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      pf IS A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the purpose with its facts is a charitable purpose` interp pf MEANS
    `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` interp (pf's purpose) (pf's facts)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 6(2) — Clarifications of the heads in paragraph (1)`

-- src:184 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1) –
-- src:185 | (a) in paragraph (1)(d), “the advancement of health” includes the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering;
-- src:186 | (b) paragraph (1)(f) includes –
-- src:187 | (i) rural or urban regeneration, and
-- src:188 | (ii) the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities;
-- src:189 | (c) in paragraph (1)(h), “sport” means sport that involves physical skill and exertion;
-- src:190 | (d) paragraph (1)(i) applies only in relation to recreational facilities or activities that are –
-- src:191 | (i) primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, or
-- src:192 | (ii) available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large;
-- src:193 | (e) paragraph (1)(n) includes relief given by the provision of accommodation or care;
-- src:194 | (f) for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p), the advancement of any philosophical belief (whether or not involving belief in a god) is analogous to the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(c).

-- 6(2)(a): "the advancement of health" includes the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering.  An extension: a purpose with that object is within head (d).
@ref Article 6(2)(a) (src:185)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(a) the advancement of health includes the purpose` facts MEANS
    facts's `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering`

-- 6(2)(b): paragraph (1)(f) includes (i) rural or urban regeneration and (ii) the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of
-- registered charities.  An extension: a purpose with either object is within head (f).
@ref Article 6(2)(b)(i) (src:187)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(b)(i) paragraph (1)(f) includes the purpose, as regeneration` facts MEANS
    facts's `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration`

@ref Article 6(2)(b)(ii) (src:188)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(b)(ii) paragraph (1)(f) includes the purpose, as promotion of civic responsibility` facts MEANS
    facts's `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities`

-- 6(2)(c): in paragraph (1)(h), "sport" means sport that involves physical skill and exertion.  A narrowing: a purpose recorded under head (h) is admitted only if the sport does.
@ref Article 6(2)(c) (src:189)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(c) sport means sport that involves physical skill and exertion` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the sport involves physical skill and exertion`
    WHEN JUST involves THEN involves
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Article 6(2)(c) was not given whether the sport involves physical skill and exertion`

-- 6(2)(d): paragraph (1)(i) applies only in relation to recreational facilities or activities that are (i) primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of age, ill-health,
-- disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, or (ii) available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large.  A narrowing: a purpose
-- recorded under head (i) is admitted only if (i) or (ii) holds.  Each fact is stated, or the clause refuses unless the other alternative already decides.
@ref Article 6(2)(d) (src:190-192)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` facts MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` (facts's `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`) THEN TRUE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as true` (facts's `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large`) THEN TRUE
        IF `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` (facts's `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`)
           AND `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` (facts's `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large`) THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `Article 6(2)(d) was not given whether the facilities or activities are primarily for people in need or open to the public at large`

@ref Article 6(2)(d) (src:190-192)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(d) both alternatives are stated as false` facts MEANS
        `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` (facts's `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`)
    AND `Art 6(2) the fact is stated as false` (facts's `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large`)

-- 6(2)(e): paragraph (1)(n) includes relief given by the provision of accommodation or care.  An extension: such relief of those in need is within head (n).
@ref Article 6(2)(e) (src:193)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` facts MEANS
    facts's `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care`

-- Any of the extensions (a), (b)(i), (b)(ii), (e) brings a purpose within a head, whatever head it was recorded under.
@ref Article 6(2) (src:184-194)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2) a clarification brings the purpose within a head` facts MEANS
        `Art 6(2)(a) the advancement of health includes the purpose` facts
    OR  `Art 6(2)(b)(i) paragraph (1)(f) includes the purpose, as regeneration` facts
    OR  `Art 6(2)(b)(ii) paragraph (1)(f) includes the purpose, as promotion of civic responsibility` facts
    OR  `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` facts

-- 6(2)(f): for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p), the advancement of any philosophical belief (whether or not involving belief in a god) is analogous to the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(c).
-- So the analogy is stated and need not be judged: such a purpose is within (p).  FORK F2.5 asks only whether it is ALSO within (c); see `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion`.
@ref Article 6(2)(f) (src:194)
GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2)(f) the purpose is analogous to the advancement of religion by the analogy of paragraph (1)(p)` purpose MEANS
    purpose's `is advancing a philosophical belief`

-- IP11 (consumed by group G8, Article 28(1)(a)): does the entity have a purpose that falls within Article 6(1)(c) itself, the advancement of religion?  A purpose of advancing a philosophical
-- belief is analogous to it by 6(2)(f), and the text says that is "for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p)": it falls within (p), not (c) (first reading, taken).  FORK F2.5.  Article 6(5) bars
-- a political purpose from every head.
@ref Article 6(1)(c), Article 6(2)(f) (src:170) (src:194)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` interp purpose MEANS
        NOT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` purpose
    AND (   purpose's head EQUALS JUST `the advancement of religion`
         OR `reading B of Article 6(2)(f): a philosophical belief is within paragraph (1)(c)` interp purpose)

@ref Article 6(1)(c), Article 6(2)(f) (src:170) (src:194)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      purpose IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reading B of Article 6(2)(f): a philosophical belief is within paragraph (1)(c)` interp purpose MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `which head a philosophical belief falls within`
    WHEN `paragraph (1)(p), by the analogy that Article 6(2)(f) states` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `paragraph (1)(c), as if the analogy made it a purpose of advancing religion` THEN purpose's `is advancing a philosophical belief`

@ref Article 6(1)(c), Article 6(2)(f) (src:170) (src:194)
@export Whether the entity has a purpose that falls within Article 6(1)(c), the advancement of religion; a purpose of advancing a philosophical belief counts only on the second reading of fork F2.5
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is which head a philosophical belief falls within
      `the entity` IS AN Entity
        @desc The entity as Article 2 leaves it; its purposes are read
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` interp `the entity` MEANS
    any (GIVEN purpose YIELD `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` interp purpose) (`the entity`'s purposes)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 6(3) — The States' power to add to the list`

-- src:195 | (3) The States may, on the recommendation of the Commissioner, by Regulations –
-- src:196 | (a) add sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1);
-- src:197 | (b) add sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2) making explanatory provision in relation to any sub-paragraphs so added to paragraph (1).
@ref Article 6(3) (src:195-197)
@export The States' permission under Article 6(3) to make Regulations adding sub-paragraphs to Article 6(1) and explanatory sub-paragraphs to Article 6(2); the power exists only on the recommendation of the Commissioner, and the content of the Regulations is not modelled here
GIVEN `the Commissioner has recommended the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the Commissioner has recommended that the States make the Regulations
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` `the Commissioner has recommended the Regulations` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has recommended the Regulations`
    THEN PARTY `the States`
         MAY `make Regulations adding sub-paragraphs to the list of charitable purposes or to its explanations` `the States`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 6(4) — The limit on the power`

-- src:198 | (4) The power under paragraph (3) does not include power –
-- src:199 | (a) to amend or restrict the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f); or
-- src:200 | (b) to alter the effect of paragraph (5).
@ref Article 6(3), Article 6(4) (src:195-200)
@export Whether Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3) as limited by Article 6(4): they must add sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1), or explanatory sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2), and must not amend or restrict paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f) or alter paragraph (5)
GIVEN content IS A `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)`
        @desc What the proposed Regulations do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` content MEANS
        (   content's `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1)`
         OR content's `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)`)
    AND (   NOT content's `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)`
         OR content's `the sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (2) make explanatory provision in relation to sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (1)`)
    AND NOT content's `amends or restricts the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f)`
    AND NOT content's `alters the effect of paragraph (5)`

@ref Article 6(3), Article 6(4) (src:195-200)
@export Whether the States may validly make the Regulations: the Commissioner has recommended them (Article 6(3)) and their content is within the power as limited by Article 6(4)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has recommended the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the Commissioner has recommended that the States make the Regulations
      content IS A `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)`
        @desc What the proposed Regulations do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` `the Commissioner has recommended the Regulations` content MEANS
        `the Commissioner has recommended the Regulations`
    AND `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` content

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§§ `Article 6(5) — Political purposes`

-- src:201 | (5) The purpose of advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election to any office, whether in Jersey or elsewhere, is neither a charitable purpose nor a purpose ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose, irrespective of whether it would otherwise fall within paragraph (1) or Article 5(1)(a)(ii).
@ref Article 6(5) (src:201)
@export Whether a purpose is excluded by Article 6(5) as the purpose of advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election, in Jersey or elsewhere; such a purpose is neither a charitable purpose nor a purpose ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose
GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose
        @desc The purpose of the entity under consideration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` purpose MEANS
    purpose's `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election`
